# Vercel Speed Insights Implementation

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for this React + Vite project following the latest official documentation from vercel.com.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- **Modified**: `package.json`
  - Added `@vercel/speed-insights` version `^2.0.0` to dependencies
  
- **Modified**: `package-lock.json`
  - Updated lockfile with new package and its 486 dependencies

### 2. Component Integration
- **Modified**: `src/App.jsx`
  - Added import statement: `import { SpeedInsights } from '@vercel/speed-insights/react';`
  - Added `<SpeedInsights />` component at the end of the main app div
  - Placement ensures the component is rendered on all pages while respecting the existing conditional Header/Footer logic

## Implementation Details

### Framework-Specific Approach
This project uses React with Vite, so I followed the React/Vite-specific installation instructions from the official Vercel documentation:
- Used the `/react` import path for the SpeedInsights component
- Placed the component in the root App component to ensure it's active on all routes

### Component Placement
The SpeedInsights component was added inside the main div after the routing components:
```jsx
<div className='font-roboto'>
  {!shouldHideHeaderFooter && <Header />}
  <Routing />
  {!shouldHideHeaderFooter && <Footer />}
  <SpeedInsights />
</div>
```

This placement ensures:
- The component is rendered on every page
- It doesn't interfere with existing conditional logic for Header/Footer
- It follows React best practices for analytics components

